{"id": "EUVD-2026-101227", "enisaUuid": "ed5fec62-89e7-369f-8aea-7775e82b3c68", "description": "L-SMASH through 2.14.5 contains a double free vulnerability in hevc_setup_first_summary() and h264_setup_first_summary() in importer/nalu_imp.c that frees borrowed codec-specific objects on error paths. Attackers can supply a crafted Annex-B elementary stream lacking a parseable SPS to lsmash_read_file() or the boxdumper, remuxer, or muxer tools, causing use-after-free, heap corruption, and crashes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:16:31", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/l-smash-hevc-importer-double-free", "https://github.com/l-smash/l-smash/blob/v2.14.5/importer/nalu_imp.c#L1356-L1378", "https://github.com/l-smash/l-smash/blob/v2.14.5/importer/nalu_imp.c#L697-L715", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/l-smash-through-2.14.5-double-free-in-hevc-and-h-264-importer-probe"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110599", "GHSA-4h8q-hwh6-8jpj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c9b94650-1617-36df-933a-5d879a46595e", "product": {"name": "l-smash", "vendor": {"name": "l-smash"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.14.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8e2d31a7-94a5-3948-982d-0ed1cd3460ab", "vendor": {"name": "l-smash"}}], "isExploited": false}